464
00:22:32,130 --> 00:22:38,040
So what is reinforcement
learning also known as RL?

465
00:22:38,040 --> 00:22:40,780
Basically it's just
trial and error learning.

466
00:22:40,780 --> 00:22:42,840
It's a very, very
general framework

467
00:22:42,840 --> 00:22:45,690
of an agent trying
to achieve a goal.

468
00:22:45,690 --> 00:22:49,260
So really, this agent learns by
interacting with an environment

469
00:22:49,260 --> 00:22:51,240
to maximize the reward.

470
00:22:51,240 --> 00:22:55,650
And I think there is sometimes a
misconception about this reward

471
00:22:55,650 --> 00:22:57,990
that has to be very
dense or it has

472
00:22:57,990 --> 00:23:00,540
to guide you towards
the solution, et cetera.

473
00:23:00,540 --> 00:23:04,440
Not at all-- in the
framework of RL,

474
00:23:04,440 --> 00:23:08,490
the reward can be basically
have I achieved my goal or not?

475
00:23:08,490 --> 00:23:11,550
So basically, in RL, we
really need to have a goal.

476
00:23:11,550 --> 00:23:15,280
But then your reward can be
goal achieved equal than 1,

477
00:23:15,280 --> 00:23:17,910
otherwise 0 all the time.

478
00:23:17,910 --> 00:23:22,000
If you don't really have a goal
that you want to try to achieve,

479
00:23:22,000 --> 00:23:25,710
